From 70fc66d4cc2abeced10ea48e5e005a10c6db142d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:15:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 58/91] ggml, llama : V4's clamped SwiGLU as one op
 (GGML_GLU_OP_SWIGLU_LIM), a prefill wave computes only its own pairs
 (SiegeLadder G8 / P5, on by default)

DeepSeek V4 / V4.1 clamp the experts' up projection to [-limit, limit] and the gate to (-inf, limit] before SwiGLU,
so the graph ran clamp, clamp, swiglu - three passes over [n_ff, n_used, n_tokens], and the fused gate/up + GLU
kernels never matched the pattern. In a prefill wave all three ran over the whole ubatch while the wave computes
only its own pairs (a twelfth of them at P11's waves of 32): SiegeLadder runs.md 4.83 / 4.94 put these passes at
more than the expert GEMMs at -ub 1536 and at 0.45 of 4.76 s of compute with P11 at 6144. Strata's GU_SWIGLU
(SiegeLadder runs.md 4.97) pointed at it.

- ggml_swiglu_lim_split(a, b, limit): silu(min(a, limit)) * clamp(b, -limit, limit) in one pass - the same
  expressions as op_clamp + op_clamp + the gated op_silu kernel, so the result is bitwise the same;
- ggml_swiglu_lim_split_ids(..., ids, skip_id): rows whose id is skip_id are neither read nor written (their
  output is undefined, as the gate / up GEMMs' rows of those pairs are; the down GEMM leaves them out the same way);
- CPU and CUDA kernels (CUDA: element-wise without ids, a block per row with them); test-backend-ops cases
  (decode and wave shapes, with and without ids - the skipped rows are gathered out before the comparison);
- llama-graph: the routed experts (with the wave's ids when the wave skips other waves' pairs) and the shared
  expert of DSV4 / DSV41 (and DFlash with hc) take it; LLAMA_DSV4_SWIGLU_FUSED=0 restores the separate ops.

SiegeLadder (bench/results/p2/swl, o34): decode exact path against the 17.10 KL base PPL 2.0990 (x1.0000), KLD
0.00000, top-1 100%, and o32's counters to the unit with text = trace; P11 at -ub 6144 on the 30K document: the
answer's top-20 log-probabilities KL 0.000000 over all 128 positions, document 110.1 -> 103.7 s (-5.8%); test4
2.2K / 8.9K prompts +1.1% / +2.4% (ABBA), the 30K consultant 269.8 -> 276.5 tok/s; decode within noise.

